apple leaks have been getting absolutely  insane over the past couple of months  and they've been getting quite a bit  weird in terms of the mac lineup that we  should be expecting this year and then  going on into next year because they're  just such different takes out there but  mark german just came out with a  bombshell report claiming that apple is  currently testing at least nine  new m2 based macs and this completely  changes the game he even says that the  new machines are already appearing in  third-party app analytics which is just  further proof for this happening and as  you know over the past few days we've  been putting out some leaked videos like  this one saying that the macbook air  2022 redesign is in deep trouble and  that was mainly based on the chance of  the redesigned macbook air getting the  old  m1 chip which i know that sounds weird  but i'm going to explain in just a  minute and then going on to a video we  put out yesterday there was a chance  that the new mac mini would come with  the m1 pro chip with a lot of evidence  for that but potentially even the m2 now  those leaks especially the macbook air  one are coming from ming chi kuo yes  he's a pretty reliable analyst and he's  been around for a very long time and the  weird thing is when last month he said  that the macbook air could come with a  new design but with the same m1 chip  which at first that made absolutely no  sense to me but he also made the leak of  where the new iphone 14 regular models  could come with the same a15 chip yes  reusing the old silicon and the reason  for that would be differences in the  pricing and of course with all the  supply chain stuff going on so if  they're willing to do this for the  iphone maybe they're also willing to  give the old macbook air the m1 chip  especially since it's a consumer based  product where people don't really care  what chip it has because the m1 is  honestly fast enough and the biggest  reason i thought this could actually  happen was because of the crazy shang  high lockdowns and just this morning  ming choco came out and he said that  apple is doing its best to negotiate  with the chinese government with the  goal of reopening suppliers production  lines that were shut down due to the  lockdown starting next week at the  earliest and he said he's not sure if  apple can succeed but it might explain  why apple supply chain has not seen any  significant order cuts due to the  lockdown so maybe apple was able to  succeed and get that open and that is a  game changer and it's part of the reason  why apple might be going forward with  the m2 chip for the max this year and of  course next year and now getting into  mark german's report on the m2 chips he  says that there are going to be at least  four different m2 base chips and there's  evidence of them inside logs within  third-party apps which is very very  important to us seeing them hopefully  soon so with that said he said these are  the new machines that we should be  expecting first of all we have a macbook  air with the m2 chip codenamed j413  and that's gonna have eight cpu cores  likely a four performance core for  efficiency core layout and then 10 cores  for the graphics that's two extra cores  compared to the current macbook air so  that's already a good piece of evidence  that this year's macbook air is gonna  have the m2 instead of the m1 which is  very reassuring  he goes on to say that the mac mini  should come with the m2 chip codenamed  j473 and that's basically going to have  the same specs as the macbook air and he  also said that there's an m2 pro  variation codenamed j474  in testing and that is likely going to  come out next year then he goes on to  say that there's going to be an entry  level macbook pro with an m2 chip  codenamed  j493 and that's also going to have the  same specs as the macbook air now to me  that seems really weird because with the  m1 macbook lineup a lot of people just  chose to buy the macbook air because it  wasn't worth spending 300 more for the  macbook pro because there weren't enough  advantages so i think this i don't know  might be a mistake by apple unless  something changes to have the same ship  with the same specs within two different  machines at two different price points  but moving on he goes on to say that the  14 inch macbook pro  will get the m2 pro and m2 max chips  codenamed  j414 and the interesting thing there is  that it's supposed to have a 12 core cpu  so i think it's gonna get two extra  efficiency cores and a 38 core gpu  that's the highest level you can get  which is really weird because the  previous one was 32 so going up to 38 is  a little bit weird i think it makes  sense to have 40 but maybe they might  just disable two of those gpu cores just  for better yields and then of course we  have the 16 inch macbook pro with  exactly the same options as a 14 inch  which makes sense because that's exactly  what we have now that's code named  j416 and then finally here's the weird  one we have the mac pro codenamed j180  and this machine will include a  successor to the m1 ultra chip used in  the mac studio so that means it's going  to be the m2 ultra now going back to  mark's report one thing he mentioned is  that apple was also testing a mac mini  with an m1 pro chip yes just like in the  video i just made yesterday the m1 pro  chip the same processor that's in the 14  and 16 inch macbook pros that one being  codenamed j374  however he is saying that maybe the mac  studio made that machine redundant and  maybe it caused apple just to cancel it  and wait for the m2 versions yes the two  that he mentions right here j473 and  j474  with the m2 chip and the m2 pro now  interestingly this actually echoes a  report from nine to five mac an  exclusive report where they were able to  find the apple is in fact working on the  m2 and the m2 pro and according to them  apple did have plans to introduce higher  end versions of the mac mini with the m1  pro and ml max chips but they were  probably scrapped for the mac studio so  that perfectly matches up to what mark  german said  and with that said we should be  hopefully getting the m2 mac mini this  year and that's exactly what mark german  said in his report saying that a new  macbook air load macbook pro and a new  mac mini are scheduled to debut as early  as this year with at least two of those  macs planned for launch around the  middle of the year so he is saying that  we should be getting the m2 chip around  the middle of the year which kind of  matches up to wwdc so that would be very  interesting because there are other  sources like bob on twitter who  admittedly does not have a good track  record but some of the stuff he said  made sense before but he believes it's  not coming at wwdc in terms of the m2  chips so i'm not sure what's going on  here but mark german definitely has  better credibility compared to this bomb  now the last thing i want to mention is  that 9-5 mac did have another exclusive  report that a new macbook air and  13-inch macbook pro are coming later  this year with the m2 chip so that  basically means that ming chukwu would  be wrong in his prediction that the  macbook air would come with the m1 ship  and also when he was saying that the mac  mini would get delayed until 2023 so i  think this is actually wrong because i  do expect a mac mini this year probably  with the m2 chip at this point even  though there is a chance that we could  get it with the m1 pro but going back to  mark german's report in his tweet i  think this does make sense especially if  apple is able to figure out all of the  supply chain issues and the lockdown  issues in shanghai  if that is true then i think we could  very well likely be seeing m2 chips  especially since there's proof of apple  testing them and working on them already  so with that said hopefully you guys  enjoyed this video and let me know your  thoughts on all these different leaks  down in the comments section below  hopefully you enjoyed it definitely  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one check out one  of those two right over there thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video

